course: dictionary
lesson: 12831
title: Enable: making things possible
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Enable» is a verb. To enable something means to make it possible for someone or something to do something. «Lungs enable us to breathe.» Without lungs we could not breathe, so lungs make breathing possible.
explain: On a computer or phone, to enable a setting means to turn it on. «To hear the video, enable the sound on your tablet» means switch the sound on so you can hear it.
explain: Look at the words around enable to work out which meaning it has. Try swapping in "make it possible" or "turn on". If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: «Enable» means to make it possible for someone or something to do something.
fact: «Enable» can also mean to turn on a setting on a computer or phone, such as «enable location».
fact: Enable someone can be informal and disapproving: it can mean helping them keep doing something bad for them.
fact: Useful phrases: enable someone to do something, enable cookies, enabled by.
fact: Verb forms: enable, enables, enabled, enabling.
exercise: «The ramp enables wheelchair users to get into the building.» What does enables mean here? | *Makes it possible | Stops them | Breaks the door | Paints the building
exercise: «To watch the video, enable the sound on your tablet.» What does enable mean? | Lose it | Break it | Turn it off | *Turn it on
exercise: «Giving him extra sweets every time he cries enables his bad habit.» What does enables suggest? | *Helps him keep doing something bad | Stops his bad habit | Hides the sweets | Finishes his homework
test: «Yesterday, the new bridge ___ people to cross the river safely.» Which word fits? | *enabled | enables | enable | enabling
test: «Please enable cookies so the website can remember your login.» What does enable mean? | Forget | *Turn on | Delete | Turn off
exam: Dad says, «The new wifi enables the whole house to watch films at once.» What does enables mean? | Breaks the router | *Makes it possible | Cleans the house | Costs more money
